<sn><md>### rclone copy

Copies files from the source to the destination.

```text
BEFORE

SOURCE                  DESTINATION
📁 Documents             📁 Backup
├── 📄 A.txt             ├── 📄 A.txt
├── 📄 B.txt             └── 📄 Old.txt
└── 📄 C.txt


COMMAND

rclone copy SOURCE DESTINATION


AFTER

SOURCE                  DESTINATION
📁 Documents             📁 Backup
├── 📄 A.txt             ├── 📄 A.txt
├── 📄 B.txt             ├── 📄 B.txt
└── 📄 C.txt             ├── 📄 C.txt
                         └── 📄 Old.txt
```

**Important:** The source remains unchanged, and extra files in the destination are preserved.
</md></sn><sn><md>### rclone move

Transfers files to the destination and then removes the successfully transferred files from the source.

```text
BEFORE

SOURCE                  DESTINATION
📁 Documents             📁 Backup
├── 📄 A.txt             ├── 📄 A.txt
├── 📄 B.txt             └── 📄 Old.txt
└── 📄 C.txt


COMMAND

rclone move SOURCE DESTINATION


AFTER

SOURCE                  DESTINATION
📁 Documents             📁 Backup
                         ├── 📄 A.txt
                         ├── 📄 B.txt
                         ├── 📄 C.txt
                         └── 📄 Old.txt
```

**Important:** Files are removed from the source only after they have been successfully transferred.
</md></sn><sn><md>### rclone sync

Makes the destination an exact copy of the source.

```text
BEFORE

SOURCE                  DESTINATION
📁 Documents             📁 Backup
├── 📄 A.txt             ├── 📄 A.txt
├── 📄 B.txt             ├── 📄 B.txt
└── 📄 C.txt             └── 📄 Old.txt


COMMAND

rclone sync SOURCE DESTINATION


AFTER

SOURCE                  DESTINATION
📁 Documents             📁 Backup
├── 📄 A.txt             ├── 📄 A.txt
├── 📄 B.txt             ├── 📄 B.txt
└── 📄 C.txt             └── 📄 C.txt
```

`Old.txt` is deleted from the destination because it does not exist in the source.
</md></sn><sn><md>### **Simple Visual Comparison**

```text
COPY
Source ──────────────► Destination
Source files: KEEP
Extra destination files: KEEP


MOVE
Source ──────────────► Destination
Source files: DELETE after successful transfer
Extra destination files: KEEP


SYNC
Source ═════════════► Destination
Source files: KEEP
Extra destination files: DELETE
Destination becomes identical to source
```
</md></sn><sn><md>### Example with MEGA

```bash
# Copy Documents to MEGA
rclone copy ~/Documents mega:Backup

# Move Documents to MEGA
rclone move ~/Documents mega:Backup

# Make MEGA Backup identical to Documents
rclone sync ~/Documents mega:Backup
```

⚠️ Before using `sync`, especially with important files, test it first:

```bash
rclone sync ~/Documents mega:Backup --dry-run
```

This shows what would happen without actually copying or deleting anything.
</md></sn>